  "question_stem": "A sprinter runs a race of $200\\text{ m}$. His total time for running the race is $20\\text{ s}$. He starts from rest and accelerates uniformly for $6\\text{ s}$, reaching a speed of $12\\text{ m s}^{-1}$. He maintains this speed for the next $10\\text{ s}$, before decelerating uniformly to cross the finishing line with speed $V\\text{ m s}^{-1}$.",
